{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1560279-mystery-cult-the-lantern-gazette","id":1560279,"title":"Mystery Cult: The Lantern Gazette","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-05-30T17:04:19-07:00","id":1560279,"title":"Mystery Cult: The Lantern Gazette","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Description: </b>A long standing underground periodical, known amongst conspiracy theorists for publishing whistleblowing news more often than not. In truth, the Guardians carefully curate the Gazette, planting just the right kernels of occult truth to get the attention of those looking into supernatural kidnappings for personal reasons. A family member who remembers their sibling being abducted by aliens, dockworkers and rangers haunted by seeing people vanish on their rounds, and even cops who were discredited as part of a supernatural cover-up are amongst the different types of people drawn into their Labyrinth. It was founded on the belief that searching for missing people that were disappeared by the supernatural is a noble pursuit, which puts Sleepers on the road to Awakening, but a very dangerous calling nonetheless. With a combination of support, oversight and well tested divination techniques, they endeavor to pave their way towards Awakening, or at the very least provide closure. Between their investigative journalism and their contact network, they tend to be well informed. In the modern age, they have established a firm presence in social media, as well as their own website, having a loyal following. Always mindful of exposing its members and informants, the Gazette uses proprietary software and servers to safeguard their identity.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Mystery Cult assets:</b> Reduce by one the Availability rating of any requisitioned Library, Contacts and Safe Place.</span></span><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table align=\"center\" class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>\u2022</b></span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><i>Reporter: </i></b>The first technique a new member is trained in is how to pick up the trail of a missing person, reopening a cold case by either finding them still alive or confirming their demise. They learn the <i>Finding</i> Ceremony (see below).<br /> \u200b</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>\u2022</b><b>\u2022</b>\u200b</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><i>Correspondent:</i></b> Being able to interview a witness or suspect is a key aspect of any finding the truth, but sometimes the case has gone cold so long that they have scattered to the four winds, or even passed away. A correspondent knows how to contact anyone, regardless of the circumstances, being well versed in the <i>Lover's </i><i>Telephone</i> Ceremony.<br /> <br /> \u200b</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>\u2022</b><b>\u2022</b><b>\u2022</b>\u200b</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><i>Producer:</i></b> Skilled in providing structure and guidance to members on the field, a producer knows how to coax leads from the spirit world itself, discovering new avenues of investigation. They receive training in the <i>Automatic Writing</i> merit. Mage members instead learn how to fine tune their Peripheral Sight, being able to quickly identify the types of magic a supernatural power falls under, developing the <i>Keen </i><i>Periphery</i> merit.<br /> \u200b</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>\u2022</b><b>\u2022</b><b>\u2022</b><b>\u2022</b>\u200b</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><i>Columnist:</i></b> A well seasoned journalist and diviner, a columnist is not only able to perceive the underlying patterns and portents around them, but also skillfully deduce new insights from them, granting them the <i>Omen Sensitivity</i> merit. A mage member's pattern recognition skills are similarly honed, allowing them to quickly relate current leads to investigations they have worked on in the past, giving them the <i>Supernal </i><i>Taxonomy</i> merit.<br /> \u200b</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>\u2022</b><b>\u2022</b><b>\u2022\u2022</b><b>\u2022</b>\u200b</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><b>Editor:</b> </i>The most veteran of all members are not only able to direct the operations of a news cycle, but they are also privy of occult techniques to read the zeitgeist around them, gaining an understanding about stories they wouldn't otherwise have, and sometimes the stories reach out to them. They gain the <i>Psychometry</i> merit. Mage members find their supernatural intuition similarly sharpened, developing the <i>Piercing Glance</i> (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) merit, allowing their senses to see past supernatural concealments<br /> \u200b</span></span></td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>New Ceremony: Finding (\u2022)</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Subject:</b> A bag.<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant, but can be repeated as needed, such as to triangulate the position of the target.<br /> <b>Symbols:</b> A piece of the target\u2019s body (at least 75% free of foreign materials such as dirt). A drop of blood, a fingernail clipping, or even a single strand of hair will suffice.<br /> <b>Ritual:</b> The ritualist places the piece of the target inside the bag and spins slowly in place while holding it in one hand.<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Occult.<br /> <b>Success:</b> The bag pulls towards the location of the target\u2019s body, whether living or dead. The ritualist intuitively knows the location of the target at the time of casting, as well as the direction and distance towards them, but does not know their location on a map.</span></span><br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>What were you thinking design wise ?</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The first tier adapts the Finding Ceremony from <i>Geist </i>1ed, but rolling Wits + Occult since it feels more thematic. The first thing new members learn is how to find where the person they are looking for is. Provided they have some of the DNA of the person they are looking for, they can find a trail even if the case has gone cold. But it's a given that with the supernatural, finding the person will not be the end of it.<br /> <br /> The second tier allows them to interview ghosts of witnesses, as well as people who are still alive but undercover, creating avenues to investigation that would otherwise not be possible.<br /> <br /> The third tier allows them to gain insights into a case that they would not otherwise have, but it requires legwork from the member, both to find a personal item of a local spirit and to interpret the clues provided. In the case of mages, they instead gain some clues on what kind of supernatural effects they are sensing, helping them deduce what it could be and aiding their investigative journalism.<br /> <br /> The fourth tier allows members to see the patterns around them, making leaps in understanding in an investigation, while simultaneously being drawn to it via the Obsessed and Spooked conditions. In the case of mages, they also become able to pick up any patterns related to other Mysteries they have investigated.<br /> <br /> The highest tier allows them to read the mental impressions in an item or area related to an investigation, and <i>Psychometry\u2019</i>s ability to be spontaneously activated means sometimes new stories can reach out to the journalists. In the case of mages, I take the merit dots that were not used in the previous tier and repurpose them to grant the best version of <i>Piercing Glance</i>, which means their keen journalistic instincts can pick up and see through supernatural concealment effects.<br /> <br /> The original concept behind them was \u201csupernatural journalists\u201d, with the hot sheets from <i>Men In Black</i> being an inspiration. In terms of feel, I was aiming for an organization a character like Fox Mulder, from the <i>X-Files,</i> would join. Utilizing divination, they would be able to pick up on leads that no one else could. Since the Geist core book explains Ceremonies as well defined occult practices that resonate with death, which anyone can learn (minor or major template), I used them for the first few tiers of mundane level merits. Afterward, I chose supernatural merits that required them to actively be on the field. Collecting an item resonant for a spirit of the area to use <i>Automatic Writing</i>, being driven towards the revelations of <i>Omen Sensitivity</i> via the Obsessed or Spooked conditions, or being incentivized to visit incident sites via <i>Psychometry </i>means the Lanterns need to be proactive. In the case of mage members, their merits focus on refining their Peripheral Sight and ability to Scrutinize, giving them stronger investigative reporter instincts. Lastly, the Mystery Cult would probably be overseen by the Guardians, since it not only serves their mission of keeping an ear to the ground to anything unusual happening in the Consilium, but would also allow them to guarantee the safety of the people that eventually come looking for anyone vanished by vampires, fae, the Seers and so on.<br /> <br /> A big thanks to NuriaAge and the Onyx Path Discord for all their feedback.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}